# Rank_Types.verse
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rank Types and Settings  -  v11  (last modified: 2026-10-24)
#
# WHAT IT DOES
#   Shared data types of the rank system: the saved player data, the rank tier and leaderboard entry structures,
#   the settings categories shown in the device's Details panel and the text helpers used by the UI.
#
# WHY IT IS USEFUL
#   Keeps all the data and settings in one place, so the device and the other files stay short and easy to read.
#
# QUICK SETUP
#   1. You do not place anything from this file: its settings appear in the Details panel of the Rank System Device.
#   2. GeneralSettings, RankThresholds, TestSettings and RankMaterials are the four collapsible categories.
#   3. Change a threshold or a material there, not in the code.
#   4. Enable DebugLoggingEnabled on the device to see the output in the Verse log.
#
# GOOD TO KNOW
#   - RankPoints and HighestRankAchieved are the only values saved for each player.
#   - The materials expect the MI_Rank_* instances of the Rank_WUI folder; keep that folder with the Verse files.
#   - Thresholds must strictly increase, otherwise the device falls back to the default ones.
#
# Author: mimmo_the_root
